  "title": "krb5: don't attempt to typedef krb5_context ourselves.",
  "description": "At least with the Heimdal Kerberos that's shipped as the NetBSD 10\nKerberos, krb5_context is typedefed as struct krb5_context_data, not as\nstruct _krb5_context. This means that !24941 broke compilation on NetBSD\n10; !24558 wasn't sufficient to fix it.",
